{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_62","type":"agent_message","text":"我会重跑 SD-6，使用两类证据：一个从默认初态出发的主链场景覆盖 `increase -> hold`，以及三个带 reachable-prefix witness 的 surrogate 场景覆盖从 `hold/decrease` 出发的 guard。这样不会把无前缀 hot-start 冒充主证据。"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_63","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"PYTHONPATH=project_1_llm_state_machine_modeling python - <<'PY'\nimport hashlib, json\nfrom dataclasses import asdict\nfrom method.schema import StageContext, TestScenario, ScenarioStep\nfrom method.stages.api import run_sd2_parse, run_sd3_semantic, run_sd4_design, run_sd5a_scenario_coverage, freeze_scenario_set, run_sd6_sim\n\nnl = '''The paper implements the single-wheel ABS hydraulic regulator as a three-state FSM coupled with a PID-based slip controller. Wheel speed and vehicle speed are used to compute the slip ratio, and the PID output drives the Stateflow supervisor instead of sending commands directly to the hydraulic valves.\n\nThe FSM contains the states \"'`increase`, `hold`, and `decrease`, where `increase` sets `k1=1, k2=0, n=0`, `hold` neutralizes both valves with `k1=0, k2=0, n=0`, and `decrease` sets `k1=0, k2=1, n=500` to release pressure.\n\nThe transition guards split the slip-error space into four bands: `increase -> hold` when `slp <= 0.01`, `hold -> increase` when `slp > 0.01`, `hold -> decrease` when `slp < -0.01`, and `decrease -> hold` when `slp >= -0.01`.\n\nThis gives a concrete discrete supervisor that maps slip-error thresholds to inlet-valve, return-valve, and pump actions while the continuous wheel-slip dynamics remain in the plant model.'\"'''\n\ndsl = '''def int k1 = 0;\ndef int k2 = 0;\ndef int n = 0;\ndef float slp = 0.0;\n\nstate ABS {\n    [*] -> increase;\n    state increase { enter { k1 = 1; k2 = 0; n = 0; } }\n    state hold { enter { k1 = 0; k2 = 0; n = 0; } }\n    state decrease { enter { k1 = 0; k2 = 1; n = 500; } }\n    increase -> hold : if [slp <= 0.01];\n    hold -> increase : if [slp > 0.01];\n    hold -> decrease : if [slp < -0.01];\n    decrease -> hold : if [slp >= -0.01];\n}\n'''\ncontext = StageContext(nl=nl, current_dsl=dsl)\nparse, pm = run_sd2_parse(dsl, context)\nsem = None\nif parse.ok:\n    sem, sm, build = run_sd3_semantic(dsl, context)\nif sem and sem.ok:\n    design, dm = run_sd4_design(context, policy_profile='generated_candidate')\nelse:\n    design = None\nscenarios = [\n    TestScenario(\n        name='default_increase_then_hold_at_boundary',\n        description='default_prefix + external_input_initial_vars: slp=0.01, first cycle enters increase, second cycle follows increase->hold.',\n        initial_vars={'slp':0.01},\n        steps=[\n            ScenarioStep(events=[], expected_state='ABS.increase', expected_vars={'k1':1,'k2':0,'n':0}, name='default_enters_increase'),\n            ScenarioStep(events=[], expected_state='ABS.hold', expected_vars={'k1':0,'k2':0,'n':0}, name='increase_to_hold_boundary'),\n        ],\n    ),\n    TestScenario(\n        name='hold_to_increase_high_slp',\n        description='reachable_prefix surrogate: default slp=0.01 reaches hold after two cycles; then external slp=0.02 drives hold->increase.',\n        initial_state='ABS.hold',\n        initial_vars={'slp':0.02, 'k1':0, 'k2':0, 'n':0},\n        steps=[ScenarioStep(events=[], expected_state='ABS.increase', expected_vars={'k1':1,'k2':0,'n':0}, name='hold_to_increase_high_slp')],\n    ),\n    TestScenario(\n        name='hold_to_decrease_negative_slp',\n        description='reachable_prefix surrogate: default slp=0.01 reaches hold after two cycles; then external slp=-0.02 drives hold->decrease.',\n        initial_state='ABS.hold',\n        initial_vars={'slp':-0.02, 'k1':0, 'k2':0, 'n':0},\n        steps=[ScenarioStep(events=[], expected_state='ABS.decrease', expected_vars={'k1':0,'k2':1,'n':500}, name='hold_to_decrease_negative_slp')],\n    ),\n    TestScenario(\n        name='decrease_to_hold_boundary_slp',\n        description='reachable_prefix surrogate: default slp=0.01 reaches hold, external slp=-0.02 reaches decrease; then slp=-0.01 drives decrease->hold.',\n        initial_state='ABS.decrease',\n        initial_vars={'slp':-0.01, 'k1':0, 'k2':1, 'n':500},\n        steps=[ScenarioStep(events=[], expected_state='ABS.hold', expected_vars={'k1':0,'k2':0,'n':0}, name='decrease_to_hold_boundary_slp')],\n    ),\n]\ncov, cm = run_sd5a_scenario_coverage(dsl, scenarios)\nss, fm = freeze_scenario_set(scenarios, source_dsl_hash='sha256:'+hashlib.sha256(dsl.encode()).hexdigest(), source_inspect_hash='sha256:'+hashlib.sha256(repr(context.inspect_json or {}).encode()).hexdigest(), source_grounding_hash='sha256:'+hashlib.sha256(nl.encode()).hexdigest(), coverage_report=cov)\nsim, simm = run_sd6_sim(dsl, ss, context)\nprint(json.dumps({\n    'sd2': {'ok': parse.ok, 'status': str(pm.status), 'error': parse.error_message},\n    'sd3': {'ok': sem.ok if sem else False, 'status': str(sm.status) if sem else None, 'error': sem.error_message if sem else None},\n    'sd4': {'ok': design.ok if design else False, 'status': str(dm.status) if design else None, 'blocking': [asdict(i) for i in (design.blocking_items if design else [])], 'advisory': [asdict(i) for i in (design.advisory_items if design else [])], 'inspect_summary': design.inspect_summary if design else {}},\n    'sd5a': {'ok': cm.ok, 'status': str(cm.status), 'output': cov},\n    'sc5f': {'ok': fm.ok, 'status': str(fm.status), 'scenario_set_id': ss.scenario_set_id},\n    'sd6': {'ok': sim.ok, 'status': str(simm.status), 'feedback': asdict(sim)},\n}, ensure_ascii=False, indent=2, default=str))\nPY\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
